Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Yes, you can write an if/then statement in C programming language as follows:
```
if (condition) {
    // code to execute if condition is true
}
```
If the condition is true, the code inside the curly braces will be executed. If the condition is false, the code inside the curly braces will not be executed.

For example, let's say we want to print "Hello" if the age of the user is greater than 18 and less than 65. We can write the if/then statement as follows:
```
if (age > 18 && age < 65) {
    printf("Hello");
}
```
In this example, the condition (age > 18 && age < 65) is true when the age of the user is between 18 and 64. The code inside the curly braces will be executed if the condition is true.
